Subject: [PATCH] The Town Map in the lower menu's panel (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Once the player has the Town Map, the panel beside the 3DS remaster's
lower menu shows it: the Town Map item's upper screen and, under it, its
guide page's description. The port draws it from the Town Map's own
pictures; the game lays it out as the Town Map app does and tells the
port (start_menu.c, StartMenu_PortSendMap):

- the sprites: the cursor and the player's head on the player's square,
  the towns' blocks (TownMap_LoadFlyLocations's colours), the places been
  through before (LoadLocationHistory's), at the Town Map's positions;
- the hidden places found, and the guide page's zoomed-in map's scroll;
- the place's name and description, printed with the game's font into
  windows off the screens and handed over through their palettes (the
  font's, the signpost's), as PrintLocationName and
  PrintLocationDescription print them.

Told again when the field starts again (ov5_021D5BC0.c), the player's
square changes or the place does. MAP and POKéTCH choose what the panel
shows (the Pokétch runs underneath all along); a tap on the map, or MAP
with the map shown, opens the Town Map app.
